# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.zed/
.vscode/
.idea/

# qlty working dirs. No trailing slash: qlty creates these as SYMLINKS into
# ~/.qlty/cache, and a dir-only pattern (`.qlty/out/`) never matches a symlink —
# which is how they came to be staged the first time qlty actually ran here.
.qlty/out
.qlty/logs
.qlty/results
.qlty/plugin_cachedir
.qlty/sources

# Claude Code local-only state
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/checkpoints/
# Per-session strike state, written by sc-strike-counter. Machine-local and it quotes the
# session's own tool calls verbatim, so it is never repo content. It went unlisted because the
# hook binaries were absent for weeks — the file only exists when the counter actually runs.
.claude/strikes.json
# The live-run marker, written by `feov-record setup` and lifted by `capture`. Machine-local
# session state naming a directory on THIS disk — the hook guards consult it to decide whether a
# run is in progress, and it means nothing in another checkout. It went unlisted for the same
# reason strikes.json did: the file only exists while a run is actually live, and none had been
# launched in this repository, so `git status` never once mentioned it.
.claude/run-live.json
.claude/spike/
.claude/*.log

# Built hook binaries + release artifacts (produced by /prosthetic-conscience:doctor or CI, never committed).
#
# The BINARIES are ignored; the DIRECTORY is not. Claude Code injects each enabled
# plugin's bin/ onto the Bash tool's PATH at ENABLE time, so a bin/ that does not exist
# when the plugin is enabled is never injected — and creating it later (which is exactly
# what doctor --fix does, ~an hour after install) does not retroactively add it. Ignoring
# the directory itself is therefore what kept every shipped binary off PATH: feov-record
# was checked by name, installed into bin/, and unreachable there. Keeping a tracked
# .gitkeep costs nothing and makes the injection possible.
plugins/*/bin/*
!plugins/*/bin/.gitkeep
plugins/*/tools/dist/
# ...and where `go build` ACTUALLY drops one. The rules above cover the INSTALL location
# (bin/) and the release staging dir; neither covers the BUILD location. `go build
# ./cmd/feov-record` run from tools/ with no -o writes the executable to tools/<cmdname>,
# and that is how a 6 MB feov-record reporting 0.17.0 sat tracked in this repo for nineteen
# version bumps, read by nothing. The policy above already said "never committed" — it just
# had no mechanism at the one path where the accident happens. scripts/pluginparity now
# fails on ANY tracked executable ANYWHERE in the repository, which catches this regardless
# of name or directory.
#
# "Anywhere" is not decoration. The guard was scoped to plugins/, and a 3.1 MB
# scripts/check.exe was committed and reached main one directory outside what it read, while
# it reported a clean board. `go build ./check` from scripts/ cannot make this mistake on
# Linux — scripts/check is a DIRECTORY, so the build refuses — which is exactly why the file
# that got through was a Windows .exe.
*.exe
#
# ...and the list of names above was itself the defect one level up. It named every binary
# that had gone wrong so far — feov-record, sc-*, gray-area, gray-area-capture — which is a
# hand-kept allowlist of the accidents already made. `go build ./cmd/seatprobe` from tools/
# dropped a 12 MB `seatprobe` straight through it, because the list could only know about
# commands that existed when it was written.
#
# What is actually true of this directory does not need keeping: Go drops a build at
# tools/<cmdname>, extensionless, and every tracked file at that level is go.mod or go.sum.
# So ignore the extensionless ones and re-admit the rest. Subdirectories are re-admitted
# explicitly — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so dropping
# that line would hide the entire source tree rather than one binary.
plugins/*/tools/*
!plugins/*/tools/*.*
!plugins/*/tools/*/
**/trajectories/agent-transcripts.tar.gz

# Agent memory is the harness's RAW ACCRUAL path (machine-local, resolved through
# CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR). The reviewed corpus that actually binds seats lives in
# feov-memory/ and is tracked; promotion between them is a deliberate review step.
# See feov-memory/red-gap-patterns/README.md.
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/gray-area/

# A RESEARCH RUN DIRECTORY IS RAW ACCRUAL TOO, and the same promotion rule applies: the run is
# working state, the corpus is what somebody decided to keep. `/research` seeds research/ with a
# live blackboard — records, shards, a marker, a dashboard regenerated every 20 seconds — and
# CLAUDE.md already calls the directory a working corpus that starts empty.
#
# THIS ONE HAS A COMMIT BEHIND IT, not a preference. ffc4bf4 deleted a tracked research corpus
# with the reason "it was test data being read as evidence" — a smoke run and a keeper are
# byte-identical in shape, so once one is committed nothing downstream can tell which it is
# reading. Ignoring the run directories makes keeping one a deliberate `git add -f`, which is the
# same shape as the .claude/agent-memory -> feov-memory promotion directly above.
research/*/
